# CRC-Based Error Detection System with ML Error Impact Predictor

## Overview

Build a robust, M.Tech-level CRC error detection and correction system in **Python** with:
1. Modular CRC Encoder/Decoder (CRC-16, CRC-32) using bitwise XOR modulo-2 division
2. Noise Injection Module (single-bit, multi-bit, burst errors)
3. ML-based Error Impact Predictor (Random Forest + XGBoost)
4. Advanced BP Decoding + ORBGRAND error correction flow
5. Comprehensive evaluation metrics and visualizations

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Language Choice**: The entire project will be implemented in **Python** (not C++). Python provides sufficient performance for simulation of 100K frames and integrates seamlessly with ML libraries (scikit-learn, XGBoost) and visualization (matplotlib, seaborn). If you need a C++ implementation for the core CRC module, please let me know.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **ORBGRAND Scope**: The ORBGRAND implementation will be a simplified simulation that demonstrates the core concept (ordered noise pattern guessing with CRC as stopping criterion). A full hardware-level ORBGRAND would require a significantly larger scope.

> [!WARNING]
> **BP Decoding**: Standard Belief Propagation is designed for codes with sparse parity-check matrices (LDPC, Polar). For CRC codes, we will implement a simplified BP-like soft-decision decoder that uses bit reliability information, and then fall back to ORBGRAND when BP fails. This follows the flowchart logic faithfully while remaining mathematically sound.

