## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Core CRC Logic

#### [NEW] [config.py](file:///c:/RISK_ASSESSMENT/CN%20MAJOR/config.py)
- Global configuration constants
- Frame sizes, number of simulations, random seeds
- Polynomial selection parameters

#### [NEW] [polynomials.py](file:///c:/RISK_ASSESSMENT/CN%20MAJOR/core/polynomials.py)
- Define standard CRC polynomials:
  - **CRC-16-CCITT**: `0x1021` (width=16, init=0xFFFF)
  - **CRC-16-IBM**: `0x8005` (width=16)
  - **CRC-32-ISO**: `0x04C11DB7` (width=32, init=0xFFFFFFFF, xor_out=0xFFFFFFFF, reflect)
- Each polynomial stored as a dataclass with: `poly`, `width`, `init`, `xor_out`, `reflect_in`, `reflect_out`

#### [NEW] [crc_encoder.py](file:///c:/RISK_ASSESSMENT/CN%20MAJOR/core/crc_encoder.py)
- `CRCEncoder` class with:
  - `encode(message_bits: List[int]) -> List[int]`: Appends CRC remainder to message
  - `_modulo2_division(dividend: List[int], divisor: List[int]) -> List[int]`: Core XOR division
  - `_reflect_bits(value: int, width: int) -> int`: Bit reflection for standard compliance
- Mathematical foundation: $T(x) = x^r \cdot M(x) + R(x)$, where $R(x) = x^r \cdot M(x) \mod G(x)$

#### [NEW] [crc_decoder.py](file:///c:/RISK_ASSESSMENT/CN%20MAJOR/core/crc_decoder.py)
- `CRCDecoder` class with:
  - `verify(received_bits: List[int]) -> bool`: Check if remainder is zero
  - `get_syndrome(received_bits: List[int]) -> List[int]`: Return syndrome for error analysis

#### [NEW] [data_framing.py](file:///c:/RISK_ASSESSMENT/CN%20MAJOR/core/data_framing.py)
- `DataFramer` class to divide raw binary data into fixed-size frames
- Support for variable frame lengths (64, 128, 256, 512, 1024 bits)

